      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1902-04-18_WidnesExaminer_art0039" n="art0039">
        <head>Ei.AMINFAit, FRID,4 k, APRIL 18 1902.</head>
        <p>Ei.AMINFAit, FRID,4 k, APRIL 18 1902.</p>
        <p>"THE CHAIRMAN."</p>
        <p>_ Alderman Flax/gamin, in proposing this toast, referred to the good behaviour of licensed victuallers to War- rington and pointed out their usefulnesa as members of the Town Council In alluding to Sir Gilbert Greenall hy expressed the hops that Sir Gilbert would follow in the footstens of his late father and become a useful mem ber of the town and benefit the trade of the country at lare.e. (applause). 'lll, CHAIRMAN briefly returned thy**.</p>
