        <p>taking a drop at goal. Walter 9oldtdoorpe had his kick charged down and Williams gaiumg possession on the wing scored h. capital try. running half the length of the field. kluzzey felled at g al. Oldham attacked immediately after the resumption. but it was not long before the Hunalet forw trds asserted them— selves, and by degrees took play to their opponents line, and Whiteley so.red at the corner. Goldthoroe's kick Gillet Later, from a scrim,nage, Robinson dodged between the opposing centres and running towards the corner flog, threw to Smith, who just ~ot over. 14okithorpe missed tho goal- kick. At the kick-off 'fophans followed up smartly, and catching the bad on the bounce scored without the liunslet men toulhing i'. Again Fitizzey failed at goal. Nothing further WM, seored, and Ilunslet came out winners by three tries (9 points), to two tries (S points).</p>
