        <p>Played at hartestown on S turday afternoon before about 500 spectators. the Kees played a reserve eleven, while Whi- ttington wure of short Alinstrnsg. The Uses won the toscand Reeves started against the hill. Wilmington assumed the ' aggressive and Reeves scored. The ['era vontinued to risonoolse the play, and a few minutes later bteeve Reeves found the net a swon time,.. beautiful dropping shot defeat- ing Rowley all the way. The Rees seemed unable to get gong and were easily held in check by the Park halves. Lyon again olayed the bail past Elow,ey but offside nullified the point Nice combination by the RAM, forwaras transferred play to the other ens, but tue moveoseat was spoiled by Flynn getting offside. The Rees eeemed to liven up at this [dine. and they caused the Cheshire teanes def use endless anxiety. From a foul close in they looks like opening their account, but Davies shot rather too high. Ali hough to bees Lad by tar the best of the play to the interval, they failed to score. Hal•-tinse—W'inniugton-Park 2 goals, St. Helens Rees nit. 'kal, Wilmington 4, Rem nil.</p>
