        <p>Trap Accident near Warrington. A somewhat, eeriou4 trap accident occurred:near Bold on Sunday evening. Mr J T Bate, a well. Warrinou Football Club, knownwsrrington ins dogcart contain- ing two women, three or four children and another rt unirenmi nbge rtPol Vitt man, when be Came into collon with Mr Ditch- field, who was driving from Penketh to St. Helens. lis is conjectnted that a Wssing motor-car frightened Mr Ditchfield's horse and caused it to swerve -to one side. Both vehicles were damaged and the occupants injured. Mr Bellian, who was returning from Liverpool in 1158 nantnr-car came upon the scene f a little later and proceeded to Dr Murray's house at Penketh for asswance. The doctor had the patients taken to the Butchers' Arms and Royal Oak lnn,where their injuries were atten- ded to. Mr Bellian afterwards called at Masan; Maginn,Bros. and ordered cabs, in which the injured were taken to their homes. One of the women received serious injuries and' several of the other occupants of the traps were cut and bruised.</p>
