        <p>WESLEYAN &amp; GENERAL ASSURANCE SOCIETY. ESTABLISHED 1541. CHIEF OFFICES: BIRMINGHAM'. (EMPOWERED BY SPECIAL ACT OF PARLIAMENT.) The SIXTY—IkIRST ANNUAL GENERAL MEETING was held at the Grand Hotel. Colmore Row, Birmingham, March 25th, 1902, Mr. JOHN FIELD, 3 P., President of the Society, in the Chair. ¶ihe following Report was present,e Your Directors have much pleasure in presenting their Report and Statement of Accounts for the year ending Decem- ber 31st, 1901. NEW POLICIES. The total number of Mcrobers ani Polley FroldErs at the close of,the year was 925,815, an increase of 69,355 on the year, after allowing for lapses, deaths and surrenders. INCOME. The Income for the year from all sources, was £535,834 4s 3d. CLAIMS. The Claims paid during the year amountito £231,691 4s 10d, which brings up the total amount paid since the Society's establisament, to £2,859,042 36 23 ASSETS. The total Assets of the Society at December 31st, amounted to £527,881 6s 93, en increase of £71,863 Is 103 on the year. The Accounts for the year have been audited, and the Securities inspected by the •Auditors appointed in aceJrciance with the Society's Rules, .who have certified to the correctness thereof. BALANCE SHEET.</p>
